# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — Known Traps

Environment and toolchain traps this project has hit. Each entry is here because it cost someone real
time, and because it fails **silently** — producing wrong behavior rather than an error.

`developer` reads this before the first change of a session. Anyone may add to it.

## Format

```
### <short name>
**Symptom** — what you see (which is usually not the problem)
**Cause** — what is actually wrong
**Fix / avoid** — what to do instead
**Found** — when, and by what
```

## Rules

- **Earned entries only.** A hypothetical trap is noise. If nobody has lost time to it, it does not go here.
- **Delete stale traps**, with a note saying why they no longer apply. A file of warnings that no
  longer bite teaches everyone to skim past the ones that do.
- **Silent failures first.** A trap that throws an error is self-documenting; one that resolves to a
  default and renders almost-correctly is what belongs at the top of this file.

